# A2ML Profile Registry

@abstract:
The verifiable index of profiles shipped by this repository (SPEC.adoc
Section 8.5). Each entry is a base record (SPEC.adoc Section 7) whose
`artefact_ref` names a profile definition and whose `hash` pins that
definition by the sha256 of its exact bytes (SPEC.adoc Section 9.2 / 9.4).
A consumer trusts a profile only when the definition's computed hash equals
the pinned hash here. This is SSOT + verifiable registry: one home per
profile (the PROFILE.a2ml file), one hash-pinned index entry (here), no
duplicated normative text.
@end

# Conventions

@rationale:
A registry entry describes a whole definition file rather than a located
region, so its `source_span` uses the file-start anchor `{1,1}-{1,1}` by
convention; the artefact is identified by `artefact_ref`. Entries carry
`provenance.kind = mechanical` because the pinned value is a mechanical fact
(the sha256 of the file) and the registry is regenerated by hashing the
definition files. Recompute with:
`sha256sum a2ml/profiles/*/PROFILE.a2ml`.
@end

